From d4221ee6c3860664a1d92eb0976288e99119a37b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: telegdyd <telegdyd93@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 04:49:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] jasmine-j0014: measure the real CPU clock

Nothing sets the Kryo 260 clocks after the bootloader (no cpufreq in the
DT, none under Linux either), and the UI is slow. osfmk/arm64/sweet_cpuclk.c
binds a thread to each CPU in turn and measures the PMU cycle counter and a
chain of dependent adds against the system counter (100 ms, interrupts
off), 20 s and 120 s after the platform expert starts. Read only;
sweetclk=0 disables it.
---
 iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetPlatformExpert.cpp |   3 +
 osfmk/arm64/sweet_cpuclk.c               | 150 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 osfmk/conf/files.arm64                   |   1 +
 3 files changed, 154 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 osfmk/arm64/sweet_cpuclk.c

